{"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/s8SendableP"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ReactorRouter","kind":"identifier"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"§22.10’s handler is ONE function from an event to one answer, which is the","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"right shape for the wire and the wrong shape for the code. A reactor"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"registered for three events opens with a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"switch"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"event.event"},{"type":"text","text":", and that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"switch is where two defects live. The first is cheap: a misspelled event name"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binds nothing and is discovered as an event that never fires. The second is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not — it is the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"default:"},{"type":"text","text":" arm that returns "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".allow"},{"type":"text","text":" on behalf of code that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"never ran, which is §22.10 rule 2’s defect relocated into user code where the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rule does not reach it."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A BUILDER RATHER THAN AN ATTRIBUTE"}]},{"type":"text","text":", and §22.14 records why: a Swift"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reactor handler is an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"type":"text","text":" closure, and collecting "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"async"},{"type":"text","text":" members by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"reflection costs a runtime dependency an SDK should not add to hand out an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute. A builder type-checks the closure against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(ReactorEvent) async throws -> ReactorAnswer"},{"type":"text","text":" at compile time, which is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stricter than what the reflection would have bought. Kotlin made the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trade for the same reason."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"PURE SUGAR."}]},{"type":"text","text":" It opens no connection, consumes no queue, verifies no event,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"signs no reply and interprets no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"timeout_ms"},{"type":"text","text":"; its output is exactly the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"handler the runtime accepts (rule 1)."}]}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/init()"]},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/boundEvents"]},{"title":"Instance Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/fallback(_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/handler()","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/on(_:_:)","doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter\/on(eventNamed:_:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/axiamsdk\/reactorrouter"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/AxiamSDK\/documentation\/AxiamSDK\/ReactorRouter","int